---Create Setup Intent
---
---Saves a buyer's payment method for later without charging it. Pass a `confirmation_token` for a method the buyer just supplied through the payment elements in setup mode, or a `payment_method_id` already on file to re-verify it. The response is the setup intent as created, not its outcome: while it is `requires_action` the buyer still has a step, so hand `client_secret` to the elements' `handleNextAction` or poll Retrieve setup status. A buyer's own token holding `member:payment_methods:use` may create a setup intent for itself from a confirmation token.
---
---`POST /setup_intents`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.setup_intents.CreateSetupIntentRequest
---@return whop.setup_intents.SetupIntent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_setup_intent(input) end

---Retrieve Setup Intent
---
---Returns one setup intent. Related records are ids — once `status` is `succeeded`, `payment_method_id` is the saved method to charge or retrieve. The buyer's own token may retrieve a setup intent that belongs to it.
---
---`GET /setup_intents/{id}`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input whop.setup_intents.GetSetupIntentRequest
---@return whop.setup_intents.SetupIntent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_setup_intent(input) end

---Retrieve setup status
---
---Retrieves how far a setup has got and what the buyer must do next, if anything. Collection runs in the background, so poll this rather than reading the create response. Accepts either a secret key or the setup's own `client_secret`, so the surface collecting the payment method can poll it directly.
---
---`GET /setup_intents/{setup_intent_id}/status`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input whop.setup_intents.GetStatusSetupIntentRequest
---@return whop.setup_intents.SetupStatus? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_status_setup_intent(input) end

---List Setup Intents
---
---Lists setup intents newest first. An account API key lists its own account; a user token lists every account it can read, or one account with `account_id`. `client_secret` is always null on list rows — retrieve the setup intent for it.
---
---`GET /setup_intents`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden.
---@param input? whop.setup_intents.ListSetupIntentsRequest
---@return whop.setup_intents.ListSetupIntentsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_setup_intents(input) end

---List Setup Intents
---
---Lists setup intents newest first. An account API key lists its own account; a user token lists every account it can read, or one account with `account_id`. `client_secret` is always null on list rows — retrieve the setup intent for it.
---
---Every page, fetched as the loop asks for it.
---
---`GET /setup_intents`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden.
---@param input? whop.setup_intents.ListSetupIntentsRequest
---@return distilled.Iterator<whop.setup_intents.ListSetupIntentsResponse>
function Client:list_setup_intents_pages(input) end

---List Setup Intents
---
---Lists setup intents newest first. An account API key lists its own account; a user token lists every account it can read, or one account with `account_id`. `client_secret` is always null on list rows — retrieve the setup intent for it.
---
---Every item of every page (`data`).
---
---`GET /setup_intents`
